{
  "id": "iconic-memory",
  "term": "iconic memory",
  "definition": "Iconic memory is a very brief form of visual sensory memory that holds what has just been seen for only a few hundred milliseconds. Its contents are organized in retina-based spatial coordinates, so during movement this short-lived image can produce visible persistence and blur rather than stable, meaningful information.",
